SELinux notes for the Motorola camera port (fogos / sm6375, Android 16)

1. Add this directory to the device tree BoardConfig:
       BOARD_SEPOLICY_DIRS += vendor/motorola/motocamera/sepolicy

2. Build, boot, launch MotCamera4, then collect denials:
       adb logcat -d | grep avc: | audit2allow -R -m motcam

3. Iterate camera.te until MotCamera4 can open all camera sensors and the
   imgtuner service (if MOTOCAMERA_IMAGERTUNING=true) starts without denials.

4. The stock MotCamera4 app declares <uses-library android:name="com.motorola.motosignature"
   android:required="true"/>, which this port provides via
   com.motorola.motosignature (dex_import) + com.motorola.motosignature.jar.
